# Copy to .env and fill in — or just run scripts/bootstrap.sh, which writes .env
# from this file with a generated gateway token, and never overwrites an existing
# one. .env is gitignored and excluded from the Docker build context by
# .dockerignore, so these never end up baked into an image layer.
#
# All values are read by OpenClaw's own ${VAR} config substitution at load time.
# The rendered ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json holds the literal ${NAME}, never the
# value. They do appear in `docker inspect` output, because compose's env_file is
# how they reach the container; see docs/plans/phase3.md.

# THE ACCESS-CONTROL BOUNDARY. Pretorin enforces this key's scopes server-side,
# and Compliance Claw deliberately does not second-guess it: the full Pretorin
# MCP tool surface is registered, and what the agent can actually do is whatever
# this key authorizes.
#   empty         -> the gateway still starts, but every platform tool fails
#   read-only     -> write tools are rejected by the platform
#   write-enabled -> the agent can write to the platform
#
# A READ-ONLY KEY IS THE DEFAULT FOR THIS POC, and it is sufficient for
# everything Compliance Claw does: bootstrap, onboarding (scripts/
# onboard-targets.sh) and assessment all work with one, because binding source
# resolvers, verifying them and provisioning recipes write only host-local state
# — the single platform call is a READ of the recommended source-kind profile.
#
# The key is operator-configurable, and a write-enabled key is an INTENTIONAL
# OPT-IN for platform writes: evidence upload, control status, risks, vendors.
# Nothing here escalates on its own. On a shared channel every user inherits this
# key's authority with no per-user attribution, so a write-enabled key needs
# user-level attribution and RBAC first.
PRETORIN_API_KEY=

# What YOU know about the key above. `pretorin whoami` reports authentication but
# not scopes, so this cannot be detected — it is a declaration, not a check.
# Read by scripts/smoke.sh only: with `read-only` it attempts a write tool and
# requires the platform to reject it; with `write` it SKIPS that probe, because
# on a write-enabled key the probe would succeed and create a real record.
PRETORIN_KEY_MODE=read-only

# Gateway auth. Required: the gateway exits 1 without it. This is the single
# authoritative token source — there is deliberately no ~/.openclaw/gateway.token
# to drift against it. scripts/bootstrap.sh generates one with
# `openssl rand -hex 32` when it creates .env.
OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN=
